#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:1
msgid "Expressions and Substitutions"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:3
msgid ""
"Various operators and function calls are supported in expressions, which may "
"be used in assignments, default recipe arguments, and inside recipe body "
"`{{…}}` substitutions."
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:7
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"tmpdir  := `mktemp -d`\n"
"version := \"0.2.7\"\n"
"tardir  := tmpdir / \"awesomesauce-\" + version\n"
"tarball := tardir + \".tar.gz\"\n"
"config  := quote(config_dir() / \".project-config\")\n"
"\n"
"publish:\n"
"  rm -f {{tarball}}\n"
"  mkdir {{tardir}}\n"
"  cp README.md *.c {{ config }} {{tardir}}\n"
"  tar zcvf {{tarball}} {{tardir}}\n"
"  scp {{tarball}} me@server.com:release/\n"
"  rm -rf {{tarball}} {{tardir}}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:23
msgid "Concatenation"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:25
msgid ""
"The `+` operator returns the left-hand argument concatenated with the right-"
"hand argument:"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:32
msgid "Logical Operators"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:34
msgid ""
"The logical operators `&&` and `||` can be used to coalesce "
"values<sup>1.37.0</sup>, similar to Python’s `and` and `or`. The only false "
"value is the empty list `[]`; every other value, including the empty string "
"`''`, is true."
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:39
msgid ""
"These operators require `set lists`<sup>1.53.0</sup>, which is currently "
"unstable."
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:42
msgid ""
"The `&&` operator returns the empty list if the left-hand argument is false, "
"otherwise it returns the right-hand argument:"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:50
msgid ""
"The `||` operator returns the left-hand argument if it is true, otherwise it "
"returns the right-hand argument:"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:58
msgid "Joining Paths"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:60
msgid "The `/` operator can be used to join two strings with a slash:"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:62
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo := \"a\" / \"b\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:71
msgid "Note that a `/` is added even if one is already present:"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:73
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo := \"a/\"\n"
"bar := foo / \"b\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:78
msgid ""
"```\n"
"$ just --evaluate bar\n"
"a//b\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:83
msgid "Absolute paths can also be constructed<sup>1.5.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:85
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo := / \"b\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:94
msgid ""
"The `/` operator uses the `/` character, even on Windows. Thus, using the `/"
"` operator should be avoided with paths that use universal naming convention "
"(UNC), i.e., those that start with `\\\\`, since forward slashes are not "
"supported with UNC paths."
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:99
msgid "Escaping `{{`"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:101
msgid "To write a recipe containing `{{`, use `{{{{`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:108
msgid "(An unmatched `}}` is ignored, so it doesn’t need to be escaped.)"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:110
msgid ""
"Another option is to put all the text you’d like to escape inside of an "
"interpolation:"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:118
msgid "Yet another option is to use `{{ \"{{\" }}`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/expressions-and-substitutions.md:120
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"braces:\n"
"  echo 'I {{ \"{{\" }}LOVE}} curly braces!'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
